WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.420
How can you measure what another mind detects?

2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.740
A baby cannot speak, and a person's report shifts with expectation.

3
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.280
Every sense also carries random fluctuation on every trial.

4
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.860
Psychophysics turns controlled trials into precise measures of perception.

5
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.940
Start by holding one response rule fixed across repeated trials.

6
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.980
A detection threshold is the smallest stimulus a person reports detecting.

7
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:36.280
A rat cannot speak, so labs measure a stand-in.

8
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.180
Calibrated von Frey filaments of rising stiffness give a withdrawal threshold.

9
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.780
Many labs use the force that lifts a paw half the time.

10
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.460
To test a baby's sight, use forced-choice preferential looking.

11
00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.980
Infants prefer a pattern to a plain field.

12
00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:59.920
A striped grating appears beside a gray field of equal brightness.

13
00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.980
An observer who cannot see which side holds the stripes judges the gaze.

14
00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:09.100
The finest grating reliably looked at gives acuity.

15
00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:13.373
Why is there always a faintest detectable stimulus?

16
00:01:14.613 --> 00:01:19.413
On each trial, responses fluctuate around their mean, with a spread measured as a

17
00:01:19.413 --> 00:01:21.153
standard deviation, SD.

18
00:01:22.893 --> 00:01:28.513
Detectability, d′, is the shift in mean response a signal causes, divided by that

19
00:01:28.513 --> 00:01:34.833
noise SD. Psychophysics pairs controlled stimuli with fixed rules to separate

20
00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:36.553
signals from noise and bias.

21
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.120
Now test your intuition.

22
00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:46.360
In 2014, Puts and colleagues measured static finger-vibration thresholds in autistic

23
00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.320
and typically developing children.

24
00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:55.080
The autistic cohort averaged 9.13 micrometres, against 6.59.

25
00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.720
Does that higher threshold show better or poorer detection?

26
00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:00.720
Puts and colleagues measured static finger vibration.

27
00:02:05.383 --> 00:02:11.603
Poorer detection. A higher threshold sounds better, yet the stimulus had to grow

28
00:02:11.603 --> 00:02:13.203
larger before it was reported.

29
00:02:14.623 --> 00:02:20.003
Subtract 6.59 from 9.13: 2.54 micrometres.

30
00:02:21.323 --> 00:02:25.883
Divided by 6.59, that is 38.5 per cent higher.

31
00:02:26.933 --> 00:02:30.253
Still, a threshold only answers what its task tests.

32
00:02:31.673 --> 00:02:37.153
Lab detection cannot measure everyday distress, and paw withdrawal is a reflex, not

33
00:02:37.153 --> 00:02:43.773
unpleasantness. Practice, repeated testing, expectation, and grader bias can also

34
00:02:43.773 --> 00:02:49.873
mislead. Guard against them with masked observers, masked grading, and randomized

35
00:02:49.873 --> 00:02:50.873
control groups.

36
00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:54.060
Those safeguards unlocked discoveries.

37
00:02:55.420 --> 00:03:01.140
In 1942, Hecht, Shlaer and Pirenne measured the faintest flashes people could see.

38
00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.140
Those flashes gave so few absorptions, spread over about 500 rods.

39
00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.500
They concluded one quantum of light, a single photon, is enough to excite a rod.

40
00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:18.800
Single toad-rod recordings showed it directly in 1979.

41
00:03:20.183 --> 00:03:26.583
In 2017, Schvartz-Leyzac, Zwolan and Pfingst tested seven adults listening through

42
00:03:26.583 --> 00:03:28.263
an implanted electrode array.

43
00:03:29.643 --> 00:03:34.523
Going from 20 active electrodes to 8 meant speech had to be louder against

44
00:03:34.523 --> 00:03:40.083
background noise. With the touch thresholds above, these results show what

45
00:03:40.083 --> 00:03:41.583
controlled trials can measure.
